1
00:00:01,125 --> 00:00:05,254
"Hark! How the bells, sweet silver bells
All seem to say, "throw cares away"!

2
00:00:05,421 --> 00:00:08,674
{\an8}"Christmas is here, bringing good cheer
ding-dong to young and old"

3
00:00:08,799 --> 00:00:11,844
{\an8}"Meek and the bold ding-dong
one seems to hear words of good cheer"

4
00:00:11,969 --> 00:00:16,098
"From everywhere, filling the air
Oh, how they pound raising the sound"

5
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:18,309
"O'er Hill and Dale, telling the tale"

6
00:00:18,434 --> 00:00:22,480
"Gaily they ring while people sing
songs of good cheer, Christmas is here"

7
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:24,690
"Merry, merry, merry, merry Christmas"

8
00:00:24,815 --> 00:00:26,859
"Merry, merry, merry, merry Christmas"

9
00:00:26,984 --> 00:00:31,155
"Hark! How the bells, sweet silver bells
All seem to say, "throw cares away"!"

10
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,783
- "Ring, ring-a-ling"
- "Ring, ding, dong"

11
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:35,826
"Ding, dong, ding"

12
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,594
We don't know if he jumped
or somebody pushed him

13
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:55,763
but he had to fall from one
of the apartments above us.

14
00:00:56,138 --> 00:00:58,933
- Any witnesses?
- No. They saw him hit

15
00:00:59,058 --> 00:01:01,102
but the crowd sure gathered fast
once he did.

16
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:05,856
Including the Attorney General's niece.
She hasn't stopped sobbing since.

17
00:01:06,065 --> 00:01:08,568
Let's process this scene quickly
get the body out of here.

18
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:09,944
You, uh, get an I.D. on it yet?

19
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,698
No. But I tell you what,
that is one fine Santa suit.

20
00:01:13,906 --> 00:01:16,158
Plush pile. Real leather uppers.

21
00:01:16,909 --> 00:01:18,202
I wish mine was that nice.

22
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:20,037
The beard appears to be real.

23
00:01:21,205 --> 00:01:24,750
Hey, Jane? Could I trouble you
for a professional opinion?

24
00:01:31,882 --> 00:01:33,884
- No.
- No what?

25
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:36,929
- This isn't the actual Santa Claus.
- Oh, really?

26
00:01:37,221 --> 00:01:40,808
Some say he doesn't exist, period...

27
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:42,768
That he's a 19th-century
marketing gimmick.

28
00:01:42,893 --> 00:01:46,689
I venture no opinion on that,
but this definitely isn't him.

29
00:01:46,814 --> 00:01:48,357
This is an impostor.

30
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:49,734
And how can you tell?

31
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:52,403
Santa would smell like reindeer
and chimneys.

32
00:01:52,528 --> 00:01:54,530
This man smells like cheap whiskey.

33
00:01:54,655 --> 00:01:59,577
Uh, excuse me. Could you, uh
reach inside that outside pocket there?

34
00:01:59,785 --> 00:02:02,079
Yeah, just there near the candy canes.
What is that?

35
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:04,540
Christmas card.

36
00:02:06,834 --> 00:02:08,502
"My life is a lie. Forgive me."

37
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,504
Well, it's not a traditional
Christmas greeting

38
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,423
but it has punch and concision.

39
00:02:12,965 --> 00:02:16,052
Very, uh, thoughtful of him
to put it in a plastic baggie for us.

40
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:18,763
- Let's us out. It's a straight-up suicide.
- Possibly.

41
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,598
But you don't think so.

42
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:23,434
Here is a man that spends
his time making kids happy...

43
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:26,437
Putting a little magic in their life,
giving them hope.

44
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:29,106
- Yeah?
- Would a man like that end his life

45
00:02:29,231 --> 00:02:31,692
making such a bloody
spectacle of himself?

46
00:02:31,817 --> 00:02:33,527
In character, in a public place

47
00:02:33,694 --> 00:02:35,529
where children are bound
to see him and spoil

48
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:38,741
their Christmases forever?
I doubt it. This was murder.

49
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,576
Okay, you may have a point

50
00:02:40,701 --> 00:02:42,536
but, you know let's keep
an open mind on this...

51
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,704
Murder.

52
00:02:48,125 --> 00:02:49,251
Happy holidays.

53
00:03:07,976 --> 00:03:09,895
Benjamin Ripple has been
a tenant here for years.

54
00:03:10,229 --> 00:03:11,522
He'd never kill himself.

55
00:03:11,647 --> 00:03:14,191
He enjoyed his life too much,
and his art.

56
00:03:14,316 --> 00:03:16,777
- His art?
- The art of being Santa.

57
00:03:17,528 --> 00:03:20,072
Benjamin lived by the traditions
of St. Nick year-round.

58
00:03:21,657 --> 00:03:23,617
{\an8}Uh, we'll take it from here. Thanks.

59
00:03:24,827 --> 00:03:26,578
{\an8}- Thank you.
- Well...

60
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:28,872
Waw!

61
00:03:31,917 --> 00:03:33,919
{\an8}Now this was a man who knew
how to sustain a moment.

62
00:03:35,879 --> 00:03:37,881
I can't believe people buy this crap.

63
00:03:38,882 --> 00:03:41,677
{\an8}I sense a Christmas
speech coming on.

64
00:03:41,802 --> 00:03:44,680
{\an8}No, I just think people can
celebrate a holy day

65
00:03:44,805 --> 00:03:47,307
without lying to children
about a magical fat guy

66
00:03:47,433 --> 00:03:48,892
with a sack full of toys.

67
00:03:49,101 --> 00:03:51,353
So you took the whole Santa
revelation badly, huh?

68
00:03:51,603 --> 00:03:53,105
Crushed my heart like a cigarette.

69
00:03:53,397 --> 00:03:55,983
{\an8}Explains why you're still looking
for magic in your life.

70
00:03:56,775 --> 00:03:58,569
{\an8}Benjamin Ripple, on the other hand

71
00:03:58,819 --> 00:04:02,448
chose to keep his childhood
beliefs very much alive.

72
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,451
He was happiest
when he was at home.

73
00:04:05,826 --> 00:04:10,038
{\an8}He felt protected,
and not so popular at school.

74
00:04:10,205 --> 00:04:11,665
{\an8}I'm guessing his parents died young.

75
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:16,253
{\an8}So to cope, he transformed
his most cherished memories

76
00:04:16,378 --> 00:04:18,464
into an identity.

77
00:04:19,298 --> 00:04:20,716
A successful career

78
00:04:20,841 --> 00:04:23,552
based on this father Christmas
fantasy chalet here.

79
00:04:23,761 --> 00:04:26,305
A career like this?
"St. Nick's picks..."

80
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:28,807
"your holiday decoration superstore."

81
00:04:29,099 --> 00:04:30,267
It's a mail order business.

82
00:04:30,726 --> 00:04:32,269
{\an8}Benjamin Ripple was a survivor.

83
00:04:32,895 --> 00:04:36,440
{\an8}- Highly unlikely he took his own life.
- So you think the suicide was staged?

84
00:04:36,648 --> 00:04:39,234
{\an8}Well, it's not to say he was
without his secrets.

85
00:04:39,359 --> 00:04:41,111
{\an8}We all have secrets, don't we?

86
00:04:42,154 --> 00:04:43,530
{\an8}And Christmas, well, it's...

87
00:04:44,156 --> 00:04:45,365
{\an8}Full of contradictions.

88
00:04:45,908 --> 00:04:48,118
The man that devoted his life
to spreading joy

89
00:04:48,243 --> 00:04:50,579
{\an8}could very likely be hiding a, uh...

90
00:04:51,121 --> 00:04:53,123
- What is that?
- What?

91
00:05:00,589 --> 00:05:01,715
A sobriety chip.

92
00:05:01,924 --> 00:05:04,176
{\an8}Still waiting on forensics,
but the coroner said

93
00:05:04,301 --> 00:05:07,513
{\an8}that Santa's blood alcohol
concentration was .45.

94
00:05:07,971 --> 00:05:10,265
- That's a lethal level.
- So much for sobriety.

95
00:05:10,557 --> 00:05:13,602
{\an8}Why would somebody kill the victim
if he was dying of booze anyway?

96
00:05:13,727 --> 00:05:15,771
{\an8}That suggests suicide, not murder.

97
00:05:15,896 --> 00:05:18,190
{\an8}So does his bank account.
I ran Ripple's financials.

98
00:05:18,315 --> 00:05:20,275
{\an8}His mail order business was hit hard
by the recession.

99
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,443
It's almost bankrupt.

100
00:05:21,568 --> 00:05:23,195
{\an8}So his business takes a dive,
Ripple starts drinking

101
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,239
{\an8}then he takes a dive straight off
his building.

102
00:05:25,364 --> 00:05:26,406
Guess again.

103
00:05:26,532 --> 00:05:28,200
I showed the suicide note
to our handwriting analyst

104
00:05:28,325 --> 00:05:30,244
compared it to attested samples
of Ripple's signature.

105
00:05:30,369 --> 00:05:32,871
{\an8}- He didn't write the note.
- And we're back to murder.

106
00:05:32,996 --> 00:05:34,206
{\an8}What else do we know about Ripple?

107
00:05:34,373 --> 00:05:38,836
Uh, he's president of something called
the national society of authentic Santas.

108
00:05:38,961 --> 00:05:40,003
What's that?

109
00:05:40,128 --> 00:05:42,798
It's a fraternal group dedicated
to the accurate portrayal of Santa Claus.

110
00:05:43,257 --> 00:05:46,009
One of Ripple's neighbors told me about it.
They're having a convention downtown.

111
00:05:46,385 --> 00:05:49,429
Rigsby, you and van pelt head over there
see what you can find out...

112
00:05:49,972 --> 00:05:53,225
{\an8}After Hightower's briefing
on the Johnson killing.

113
00:05:53,517 --> 00:05:55,727
What does she have to brief us for?
Someone torched a cop killer.

114
00:05:55,894 --> 00:05:57,396
It happened in our house.
It's not right.

115
00:05:57,521 --> 00:05:59,064
He was a cop killer. Good riddance.

116
00:05:59,231 --> 00:06:01,859
Yeah, okay, zip it if you know
what's good for you.

117
00:06:03,902 --> 00:06:05,612
Walk over.
I'm gonna go round up Jane.

118
00:06:08,782 --> 00:06:12,452
{\an8}Two days ago
a suspect was doused in an accelerant

119
00:06:12,786 --> 00:06:15,747
and set alight in a CBI holding cell.

120
00:06:15,956 --> 00:06:20,711
This was not karma,
rough justice, payback.

121
00:06:20,919 --> 00:06:22,588
This was a criminal act.

122
00:06:23,046 --> 00:06:26,967
The homicide investigation
will be led by J.J. LaRoche

123
00:06:27,092 --> 00:06:29,011
the new head of our professional
standards unit.

124
00:06:30,429 --> 00:06:31,471
Thank you.

125
00:06:32,222 --> 00:06:33,891
Who the hell is J.J. LaRoche?

126
00:06:36,143 --> 00:06:37,561
- Excuse me.
- Sorry.

127
00:06:43,483 --> 00:06:44,860
Thank you, Ms. Hightower.

128
00:06:48,947 --> 00:06:52,242
It's very likely that one of you
people here in this room

129
00:06:52,534 --> 00:06:53,660
is the murderer.

130
00:06:54,494 --> 00:06:55,746
You know who you are.

131
00:06:57,122 --> 00:06:58,624
Okay, lights, please.

132
00:07:01,209 --> 00:07:02,920
We're going to run through
the facts now...

133
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:06,757
So that we are all on the same page.

134
00:07:10,385 --> 00:07:13,263
The victim was Todd Johnson.

135
00:07:13,764 --> 00:07:14,806
E.M.T.

136
00:07:15,265 --> 00:07:17,726
Responsible for killing six policemen

137
00:07:18,018 --> 00:07:21,021
and a young woman, that we know of.

138
00:07:25,984 --> 00:07:27,569
Our updated security system

139
00:07:27,694 --> 00:07:31,406
has provided me
with a very accurate list

140
00:07:31,698 --> 00:07:35,202
of everybody who was in this building
at the time of the murder.

141
00:07:35,744 --> 00:07:37,037
This guy should charge admission.

142
00:07:37,204 --> 00:07:41,458
I will be talking selectively
with some of you on the list

143
00:07:42,209 --> 00:07:43,251
over the next days

144
00:07:43,377 --> 00:07:47,172
my people will be taking blood,
hair, and tissue samples

145
00:07:47,297 --> 00:07:49,091
from everybody on the list.

146
00:07:49,341 --> 00:07:52,886
Your cooperation is expected
and appreciated.

147
00:07:53,095 --> 00:07:55,013
- Uh, excuse me.
- Yes.

148
00:07:55,222 --> 00:07:56,348
Why the samples?

149
00:08:00,477 --> 00:08:01,520
What's your name?

150
00:08:02,479 --> 00:08:03,647
Wayne Rigsby.

151
00:08:07,526 --> 00:08:08,568
Wayne...

152
00:08:09,653 --> 00:08:16,118
Wayne... We need the samples...
To test for accelerants.

153
00:08:18,328 --> 00:08:19,579
Thank you for your interest.

154
00:08:22,124 --> 00:08:23,333
Any other questions?

155
00:08:54,239 --> 00:08:55,907
Tyger, Tyger...

156
00:09:08,211 --> 00:09:09,504
You remembered something.

157
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:15,260
- Did I?
- Yes, you did. What was it?

158
00:09:15,677 --> 00:09:18,889
The smell of a man burning.
Do you know that smell?

159
00:09:19,056 --> 00:09:21,099
Yes. Very like barbecue.

160
00:09:21,516 --> 00:09:24,686
But we both know that's not
what I'm referring to.

161
00:09:25,771 --> 00:09:26,813
A lighter.

162
00:09:28,982 --> 00:09:30,984
I opened the door, Todd was on fire

163
00:09:31,109 --> 00:09:33,320
and there was a green lighter
on the bench.

164
00:09:34,863 --> 00:09:37,199
But it wasn't in the evidence report.

165
00:09:38,617 --> 00:09:41,328
- You read the evidence report.
- Oh, more like skimmed.

166
00:09:41,495 --> 00:09:43,330
You know, those things are not exactly
summer reading

167
00:09:43,455 --> 00:09:45,874
but I get paid to consult, so skim I do.

168
00:09:52,214 --> 00:09:54,508
It's on its way to the FBI crime lab.

169
00:09:54,758 --> 00:09:56,093
- May I?
- No.

170
00:09:59,679 --> 00:10:02,057
I won't be needing your consultation
on this case.

171
00:10:03,183 --> 00:10:05,435
But you and I will talk this afternoon.

172
00:10:05,685 --> 00:10:06,895
Look forward to it.

173
00:10:20,492 --> 00:10:22,619
Wow. Santapalooza.

174
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:26,623
For Santa Henry's social media
workshop at 3:00.

175
00:10:26,748 --> 00:10:29,042
And, uh, don't forget to buy
your raffle tickets

176
00:10:29,292 --> 00:10:31,044
for the jingle ball tonight.

177
00:10:31,753 --> 00:10:33,255
Oh, hi. I'm Bob. Can I help you?

178
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:36,174
Agent Wayne Rigsby.
This is Agent van pelt. We're from CBI.

179
00:10:36,383 --> 00:10:38,135
Oh, you're here about Benjamin.

180
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:42,097
He should be up here, not me.

181
00:10:42,222 --> 00:10:44,724
I mean, we're just all trying
to move ahead here.

182
00:10:44,891 --> 00:10:47,394
- It's what he'd want.
- Were you close with the victim?

183
00:10:47,561 --> 00:10:50,272
- Yes, I was. Um, we all were...
- Liar!

184
00:10:52,566 --> 00:10:53,859
You hated Benjamin.

185
00:10:54,442 --> 00:10:56,111
You were trying to kick
him out of office.

186
00:10:56,361 --> 00:10:59,030
Well, congratulations.
You got what you wanted.

187
00:10:59,197 --> 00:11:00,240
And you are?

188
00:11:00,949 --> 00:11:01,992
Tony.

189
00:11:02,742 --> 00:11:06,246
And that man had a vendetta against Benjamin
because he wanted to open our doors

190
00:11:06,371 --> 00:11:08,665
to Santas of all races,
creeds, and colors.

191
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:10,709
Which will never happen.

192
00:11:12,669 --> 00:11:15,088
Look, if Santa isn't white, male,
and Christian

193
00:11:15,213 --> 00:11:17,632
- then what the heck is he?
- He's everyone.

194
00:11:17,841 --> 00:11:19,968
He's the spirit of generosity
in all of us.

195
00:11:20,093 --> 00:11:22,554
- He's the...
- Oh, would you be quiet, you dumb hippie?

196
00:11:23,555 --> 00:11:26,975
Hey! Hey! Okay, let's just...
Let's just go for a little drive, shall we?

197
00:11:28,435 --> 00:11:30,645
Everything's fine. Just... carry on.

198
00:11:34,191 --> 00:11:35,233
Happy Hanukkah.

199
00:11:36,193 --> 00:11:37,444
Feliz Navidad.

200
00:11:49,873 --> 00:11:53,001
- Where's Patrick Jane?
- In the field.

201
00:11:55,003 --> 00:11:56,338
That's inconvenient.

202
00:12:00,342 --> 00:12:03,553
- I'm sorry. Is there a problem?
- Yes.

203
00:12:04,262 --> 00:12:08,016
Jane is the lead suspect in my investigation
and I can't find him.

204
00:12:09,351 --> 00:12:10,852
Jane's your lead suspect?

205
00:12:12,687 --> 00:12:13,813
You smile.

206
00:12:15,523 --> 00:12:19,861
- You think he's not capable of murder?
- He's capable.

207
00:12:20,403 --> 00:12:23,865
I'm smiling because it's an absurd idea,
Jane killing Johnson.

208
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:26,201
He caught him.
He put him in that cell.

209
00:12:26,326 --> 00:12:29,079
He was the last person to see him
alive in that cell.

210
00:12:29,287 --> 00:12:30,705
And I was next to last.

211
00:12:31,539 --> 00:12:33,959
Look, Johnson asked to speak
with Jane.

212
00:12:34,084 --> 00:12:36,419
He said he had a secret
he wouldn't tell anyone else.

213
00:12:36,544 --> 00:12:39,047
Jane didn't wanna see him.
I made him go.

214
00:12:39,506 --> 00:12:41,800
The guy was on fire
when he opened the cell door.

215
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:46,471
- Why would Jane kill him?
- That's what I shall ask him...

216
00:12:48,098 --> 00:12:49,140
When I find him.

217
00:12:51,351 --> 00:12:53,728
- Hey, Lisbon.
- "Uh, LaRoche is looking for you."

218
00:12:53,937 --> 00:12:55,188
Oh. Wish him luck.

219
00:12:55,522 --> 00:12:58,566
Jane, you don't want to rile this one up.
You should probably come in.

220
00:12:58,775 --> 00:13:01,319
"Uh, did you track down Ripple's
alcohol recovery group?"

221
00:13:01,736 --> 00:13:03,530
Well, I think I found
what I'm looking for.

222
00:13:03,655 --> 00:13:04,698
Gotta go!

223
00:13:12,914 --> 00:13:13,999
Hey, Virgil.

224
00:13:15,917 --> 00:13:16,960
Patrick.

225
00:13:17,627 --> 00:13:18,837
What are you doing here?

226
00:13:19,254 --> 00:13:21,006
Your old assistant told me
where to find you.

227
00:13:22,173 --> 00:13:23,925
- I need your help.
- Well, that's a twist.

228
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:25,844
You never needed my help
when I was your boss.

229
00:13:26,219 --> 00:13:28,179
What help could I be now?

230
00:13:28,305 --> 00:13:30,724
A cop-killer burned alive
in CBI custody.

231
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:32,058
I heard.

232
00:13:32,892 --> 00:13:35,145
Listen, if it's anything to do
with that, I don't wanna...

233
00:13:35,270 --> 00:13:37,147
Whoever set the fire works
for Red John.

234
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:39,733
Jane...

235
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:42,819
He was a member of
Red John's network.

236
00:13:43,153 --> 00:13:46,865
And another member of his network
killed him to stop him from talking.

237
00:13:47,073 --> 00:13:51,119
But here's the thing...
Red John doesn't know I know that.

238
00:13:51,703 --> 00:13:53,872
For the first time,
I have the advantage.

239
00:13:54,873 --> 00:13:58,793
- You sound nuts, my friend.
- No, this is real.

240
00:13:59,336 --> 00:14:03,089
If I can find who killed Todd Johnson
I can trace them back to Red John.

241
00:14:03,214 --> 00:14:05,216
I need LaRoche's suspect list

242
00:14:05,383 --> 00:14:09,721
which you, with all your back-channel
contacts, can get me.

243
00:14:11,765 --> 00:14:16,269
- What does Lisbon think of your theory?
- I can't tell her. That'd put her at risk.

244
00:14:16,478 --> 00:14:17,729
Of course.

245
00:14:18,355 --> 00:14:19,647
And what about me?

246
00:14:19,773 --> 00:14:21,608
You're a brave old man
with nothing to lose.

247
00:14:22,817 --> 00:14:26,112
Not so brave.
Not so old.

248
00:14:26,905 --> 00:14:29,324
What do you say?
Will you help me?

249
00:14:30,325 --> 00:14:31,868
You need a different kind of help.

250
00:14:32,744 --> 00:14:36,206
Red John has turned you
into a paranoid conspiracy freak.

251
00:14:37,916 --> 00:14:40,293
This from a guy on a pier
with two 40s under his chair

252
00:14:40,418 --> 00:14:41,795
and no fish in his bucket?

253
00:14:42,253 --> 00:14:44,881
- You're not even using the right bait.
- Am so.

254
00:14:46,925 --> 00:14:48,259
What do you do when you catch one?

255
00:14:48,426 --> 00:14:50,637
- Depends on what kind of fish it is.
- No.

256
00:14:51,137 --> 00:14:53,306
When you catch one,
no matter what kind it is

257
00:14:53,515 --> 00:14:57,936
you will stop and you will look at it
at this piece of life that you destroyed

258
00:14:58,061 --> 00:14:59,104
and you will think to yourself

259
00:14:59,229 --> 00:15:02,148
"what the hell am I doing here,
a drunken fish-killer"

260
00:15:02,857 --> 00:15:04,359
"when I could be doing
something useful?"

261
00:15:04,484 --> 00:15:05,527
And then you'll call me.

262
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:23,893
You two should be
ashamed of yourselves.

263
00:15:24,435 --> 00:15:26,437
You, with the grudge,
where were you last night?

264
00:15:27,063 --> 00:15:28,564
Having some drinks with the guys.

265
00:15:29,148 --> 00:15:30,191
They were plotting ways

266
00:15:30,316 --> 00:15:32,693
- to replace Benjamin as president.
- How would you know?

267
00:15:32,985 --> 00:15:34,028
Is it true?

268
00:15:35,363 --> 00:15:37,031
Look, I'm head of
the steering committee.

269
00:15:37,573 --> 00:15:40,076
Benjamin was using our society
as a platform

270
00:15:40,201 --> 00:15:42,245
to promote his online business.

271
00:15:42,578 --> 00:15:44,330
And how'd you know what they
were talking about last night?

272
00:15:44,497 --> 00:15:47,542
I was sitting two stools away
at the hotel bar.

273
00:15:47,792 --> 00:15:50,002
They had no idea who I was
without the beard.

274
00:15:50,127 --> 00:15:51,546
Oh, gee, a spy!

275
00:15:51,671 --> 00:15:54,048
A concerned member of the N.S.A.S.

276
00:15:54,674 --> 00:15:56,425
They were trying to take
over his position.

277
00:15:57,051 --> 00:15:59,262
And they were drooling over his date.

278
00:15:59,804 --> 00:16:03,015
- The victim had a date at the bar?
- No, at the opening night mixer.

279
00:16:03,474 --> 00:16:06,936
- An attractive young woman.
- You called her his ho-ho-ho.

280
00:16:07,061 --> 00:16:09,939
Oh, come on. You can't tell me
that Benjamin didn't pay for her

281
00:16:10,064 --> 00:16:11,691
with the proceeds from
that online superstore

282
00:16:11,816 --> 00:16:12,984
that he built on our backs!

283
00:16:13,109 --> 00:16:14,694
Either of you happen to catch
the name of this woman?

284
00:16:15,152 --> 00:16:16,195
- Roxy.
- Roxy.

285
00:16:20,658 --> 00:16:24,787
So, we were all close to Benjamin.

286
00:16:28,499 --> 00:16:31,210
I was his sponsor for ten years.

287
00:16:31,961 --> 00:16:35,798
But really, he helped me up.

288
00:16:40,052 --> 00:16:43,723
It's okay, I'm okay. Thanks.

289
00:16:44,932 --> 00:16:46,183
Let's just forge ahead.

290
00:16:48,811 --> 00:16:51,897
Are there any newcomers
in their first few days of sobriety

291
00:16:52,023 --> 00:16:53,232
who would like a welcome chip?

292
00:17:00,489 --> 00:17:01,532
Why not?

293
00:17:04,535 --> 00:17:06,037
Oh, okay.

294
00:17:06,162 --> 00:17:07,496
Thank you very... Thank you.

295
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,582
- Okay.
- Welcome!

296
00:17:15,463 --> 00:17:17,006
Guess I'll be a newcomer every day.

297
00:17:19,050 --> 00:17:22,178
It's customary to introduce yourself.
First name only.

298
00:17:23,137 --> 00:17:25,389
- Patrick.
- Hi, Patrick.

299
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:26,682
Hi, folks.

300
00:17:27,224 --> 00:17:29,727
Anybody who can sponsor Patrick,
please raise your hand.

301
00:17:31,312 --> 00:17:32,355
Would you?

302
00:17:34,482 --> 00:17:35,941
Sure. Sure.

303
00:17:36,067 --> 00:17:38,277
Um, of... of course. I'd be happy to.

304
00:17:38,903 --> 00:17:39,945
Thank you.

305
00:17:40,196 --> 00:17:42,031
Would you like to share, Patrick?

306
00:17:43,199 --> 00:17:47,912
Uh, no, I'm not... I'm not ready to share.
Not yet, thanks.

307
00:17:48,412 --> 00:17:50,665
Well, nobody will think less of you
if you don't

308
00:17:50,790 --> 00:17:53,751
but you won't find a more supportive
group than we are.

309
00:17:55,044 --> 00:17:56,087
We all...

310
00:17:56,379 --> 00:18:00,591
Find relief in sharing our...
our daily struggle with addiction.

311
00:18:00,841 --> 00:18:03,511
Well, to be perfectly honest,
I'm not an addict.

312
00:18:06,055 --> 00:18:07,223
I, um...

313
00:18:08,641 --> 00:18:09,684
Well, that's...

314
00:18:13,813 --> 00:18:15,856
That's not strictly true.
I do have an addiction.

315
00:18:17,358 --> 00:18:18,442
Go on.

316
00:18:19,694 --> 00:18:20,945
You're safe here.

317
00:18:22,738 --> 00:18:23,781
It, um...

318
00:18:24,323 --> 00:18:25,491
Destroyed my family.

319
00:18:28,953 --> 00:18:31,330
But I-I c... I can't talk about it. I...

320
00:18:31,706 --> 00:18:32,832
It's not that I don't want to.

321
00:18:32,957 --> 00:18:35,126
It's just, I have so many bad things
in my head that I'd...

322
00:18:35,501 --> 00:18:37,044
Like to throw out, I just...

323
00:18:43,384 --> 00:18:46,178
If I start talking about it...

324
00:18:54,270 --> 00:18:55,312
I...

325
00:18:56,021 --> 00:18:57,648
Just don't know that I'll be able to stop.

326
00:19:00,568 --> 00:19:01,610
Excuse me.

327
00:19:07,199 --> 00:19:08,826
Anybody else wanna share?

328
00:19:12,913 --> 00:19:13,998
What are you doing here?

329
00:19:14,832 --> 00:19:15,875
Watching you.

330
00:19:18,586 --> 00:19:20,713
You have substance
abuse issues, Patrick?

331
00:19:21,046 --> 00:19:24,550
- There's no tag for that in your files.
- I'm on a case.

332
00:19:26,093 --> 00:19:28,262
You're telling me those words back
there... They weren't real?

333
00:19:28,387 --> 00:19:31,557
- I mean, you're sweating.
- Simple parlor trick.

334
00:19:32,266 --> 00:19:34,602
With biofeedback, you can train
your mind to control

335
00:19:34,727 --> 00:19:37,563
involuntary body processes...
heart rate, blood pressure...

336
00:19:38,063 --> 00:19:39,106
Temperature.

337
00:19:39,774 --> 00:19:42,860
- I'm glad you enjoyed the performance.
- So you're working undercover?

338
00:19:43,068 --> 00:19:45,112
Which you just blew for me.
Thank you very much.

339
00:19:45,321 --> 00:19:46,655
Well, I doubt that.

340
00:19:47,573 --> 00:19:50,326
Up to the moment you left,
you had them transfixed.

341
00:19:52,995 --> 00:19:54,038
What's that like...

342
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:58,417
- Such power over people?
- You tell me.

343
00:19:59,335 --> 00:20:04,715
I expect this Robocop routine of yours
normally works quite effectively.

344
00:20:06,342 --> 00:20:07,384
Normally.

345
00:20:08,719 --> 00:20:12,681
But you seem immune,
so I may have to step up my efforts.

346
00:20:14,433 --> 00:20:18,145
Or we could go back to CBI right now
and conduct the interview you owe me.

347
00:20:18,771 --> 00:20:22,274
- Patrick? Everything okay?
- Yeah, I was just getting some air.

348
00:20:22,399 --> 00:20:24,109
- Okay
- I'll come back in now.

349
00:20:35,454 --> 00:20:37,456
How was Ripple's A.A. group?
Did you learn anything?

350
00:20:37,706 --> 00:20:39,875
Yes. They're very big on hugs.

351
00:20:40,251 --> 00:20:41,335
About the victim?

352
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:44,046
Well, I'll learn more tomorrow
when I speak with his sponsor

353
00:20:44,171 --> 00:20:45,673
who is now my sponsor, too.

354
00:20:46,674 --> 00:20:49,677
May Walters. Lovely lady...
or a killer. I can't tell.

355
00:20:49,885 --> 00:20:52,179
- You went undercover?
- Yes.

356
00:20:52,304 --> 00:20:54,765
- Why is that so hard to accept?
- You never go undercover.

357
00:20:54,974 --> 00:20:58,686
Precisely. I wanted to have some fun,
just like you guys seem to.

358
00:20:59,228 --> 00:21:00,855
Anything on the other Santas?

359
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:04,108
Santa Bob has motive.
I'm running down his alibi.

360
00:21:05,150 --> 00:21:06,402
They did give us a new lead.

361
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:11,156
- Hello, Roxy Rhodes.
- Real name... Roxanne Rabinovich.

362
00:21:11,282 --> 00:21:13,325
No record, but she works
at an elite escort service.

363
00:21:13,450 --> 00:21:15,160
Spent an evening with the victim
the night before he died.

364
00:21:15,536 --> 00:21:17,955
- Whoa. Santa got some naughty this year.
- Yeah.

365
00:21:18,205 --> 00:21:20,457
- We should bring her in here tomorrow.
- Yeah, I can question her.

366
00:21:20,666 --> 00:21:22,418
- It's my lead.
- Just offering to help out.

367
00:21:23,127 --> 00:21:24,670
- All right.
- We have a situation.

368
00:21:25,004 --> 00:21:26,380
Someone broke into Ripple's apartment.

369
00:21:30,801 --> 00:21:32,344
Two hours after we cleared
the crime scene

370
00:21:32,469 --> 00:21:33,679
we get a call from a neighbor

371
00:21:34,138 --> 00:21:36,348
says she hears a lot of crashing
inside the apartment.

372
00:21:37,433 --> 00:21:38,934
Looks like they were
looking for something.

373
00:21:41,103 --> 00:21:42,271
Any signs of forced entry?

374
00:21:42,646 --> 00:21:44,273
None. We think
somebody had the key.

375
00:21:44,773 --> 00:21:46,233
Must have been one of the elves.

376
00:21:52,137 --> 00:21:53,180
Do you know this man?

377
00:21:53,764 --> 00:21:56,850
Sure. Benjamin. We hung out.

378
00:21:57,142 --> 00:21:58,519
He was murdered two days ago.

379
00:22:01,396 --> 00:22:02,439
Okay.

380
00:22:02,564 --> 00:22:06,527
- You don't seem very broken up over this.
- Why should I be? I don't marry them.

381
00:22:07,152 --> 00:22:09,613
Just provide a standard G.F.E.

382
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:11,824
- G.F.E.?
- Girlfriend experience.

383
00:22:13,450 --> 00:22:15,577
I'm paid to show up
and act like I like them

384
00:22:15,744 --> 00:22:18,413
but I don't get emotionally
involved with clients.

385
00:22:18,705 --> 00:22:20,624
That way madness lies, you know?

386
00:22:20,791 --> 00:22:23,085
- And Ripple was a client.
- No...

387
00:22:23,210 --> 00:22:24,670
But you were his date
at the Santa convention?

388
00:22:25,712 --> 00:22:28,465
- I was paid by someone else.
- And how does that work?

389
00:22:28,590 --> 00:22:31,927
I'm paid to attend A.A. meetings
and recovery groups

390
00:22:32,052 --> 00:22:33,428
and recruit patients.

391
00:22:33,595 --> 00:22:36,890
- Patients for what?
- This man, Jack Wilder.

392
00:22:37,683 --> 00:22:40,394
He owns a treatment facility
for alcohol addiction.

393
00:22:41,186 --> 00:22:44,648
Very exclusive.
Only the financially secure can afford it.

394
00:22:44,773 --> 00:22:45,816
So let me get this straight...

395
00:22:45,941 --> 00:22:48,360
Wilder hires you to cruise A.A. meetings
looking for rich drunks?

396
00:22:49,069 --> 00:22:51,196
I meet 'em, chat 'em up, and tell them

397
00:22:51,321 --> 00:22:54,616
about this miraculous treatment
facility that changed my life.

398
00:22:54,741 --> 00:22:55,993
So you underwent the treatment?

399
00:22:56,827 --> 00:23:00,163
No. Tequila is my dear friend.

400
00:23:00,747 --> 00:23:03,208
But that doesn't mean the center
didn't change my life.

401
00:23:03,542 --> 00:23:04,877
You should see my new Jaguar.

402
00:23:07,004 --> 00:23:08,046
No doubt.

403
00:23:08,589 --> 00:23:09,840
Do you have an address for Wilder?

404
00:23:10,507 --> 00:23:13,093
You were very brave yesterday
sharing like that.

405
00:23:13,427 --> 00:23:16,763
Nah. You were in love
with Benjamin, weren't you?

406
00:23:18,849 --> 00:23:22,019
It's why the program doesn't
encourage opposite-sex sponsors.

407
00:23:22,185 --> 00:23:23,979
But he didn't return the feelings.

408
00:23:25,355 --> 00:23:26,607
I think he did...

409
00:23:27,274 --> 00:23:28,358
In his own way.

410
00:23:30,068 --> 00:23:32,905
But Benjamin had his priorities.

411
00:23:33,030 --> 00:23:34,072
The red suit.

412
00:23:34,197 --> 00:23:38,493
I imagine that left you feeling ignored?
Alone? Angry?

413
00:23:38,619 --> 00:23:40,954
- Got that right.
- Angry enough to destroy his home?

414
00:23:43,999 --> 00:23:46,376
- Who are you?
- I'm a consultant for the CBI.

415
00:23:46,501 --> 00:23:48,211
We're investigating Benjamin's murder.

416
00:23:48,420 --> 00:23:52,257
- You lied about your addiction?
- No. That's real enough, I suppose.

417
00:23:53,425 --> 00:23:55,093
Where were you the night Benjamin
was killed?

418
00:23:55,552 --> 00:23:57,346
Alone in my apartment.

419
00:23:57,554 --> 00:24:00,515
May, they're gonna treat you
like a suspect.

420
00:24:00,641 --> 00:24:02,059
You destroyed their crime scene.

421
00:24:02,517 --> 00:24:03,977
I went there to find something.

422
00:24:05,354 --> 00:24:07,356
You know, to...
to remember Benjamin by?

423
00:24:08,607 --> 00:24:10,943
When I saw the decorations, I-I got mad.

424
00:24:12,402 --> 00:24:13,654
Santa was...

425
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:17,074
Was another form of addiction
for Benjamin.

426
00:24:17,824 --> 00:24:21,119
Any time anything cuts you off
from experiencing your life

427
00:24:21,244 --> 00:24:24,122
- It's unhealthy, right?
- Wouldn't know.

428
00:24:24,498 --> 00:24:27,918
Last week
for the first time in ten years

429
00:24:28,043 --> 00:24:29,586
he took a shot of vodka.

430
00:24:31,755 --> 00:24:33,340
It crushed both of us.

431
00:24:36,635 --> 00:24:38,512
Is this what you were looking for
in Benjamin's apartment?

432
00:24:46,979 --> 00:24:48,438
Best ten years of my life.

433
00:24:59,825 --> 00:25:02,953
Jack Wilder, behavioral therapist.
Sorry to keep you waiting.

434
00:25:03,078 --> 00:25:05,664
Agent Lisbon, Van Pelt.
We're with the CBI.

435
00:25:05,831 --> 00:25:08,166
We came to see if Benjamin Ripple
was a patient here.

436
00:25:10,002 --> 00:25:13,088
Uh, you know what?
Let's talk about this in my office.

437
00:25:14,548 --> 00:25:18,093
This is a licensed medical facility, ladies.

438
00:25:18,218 --> 00:25:20,137
My client list is privileged.

439
00:25:20,262 --> 00:25:21,304
Are you a doctor?

440
00:25:21,722 --> 00:25:23,306
Technically, no,
but I do have a license...

441
00:25:23,432 --> 00:25:26,101
Well, this is a homicide investigation.
You're a suspect.

442
00:25:26,226 --> 00:25:27,519
There is no privilege here.

443
00:25:27,811 --> 00:25:30,480
Homicide? Benjamin's dead?

444
00:25:30,856 --> 00:25:32,858
With enough alcohol in his system
to kill an elephant.

445
00:25:33,316 --> 00:25:35,485
A girl from an escort service says
that you paid her

446
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:37,821
to steer Benjamin to your clinic.
Is that correct?

447
00:25:37,988 --> 00:25:41,324
That's impossible. My clients would never
take a drink so soon after treatment.

448
00:25:41,450 --> 00:25:43,035
- When did he die?
- Two nights ago.

449
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,494
When did you treat him?

450
00:25:46,872 --> 00:25:47,914
Two nights ago.

451
00:25:51,043 --> 00:25:53,545
Aversion therapy can be used
to treat any bad habit...

452
00:25:53,754 --> 00:25:57,549
Uh, smoking, alcoholism,
gambling, violence...

453
00:25:58,258 --> 00:25:59,509
Sexual deviancy.

454
00:26:00,302 --> 00:26:03,472
My methods are based
on classical conditioning techniques.

455
00:26:03,805 --> 00:26:04,848
Please.

456
00:26:06,767 --> 00:26:09,019
I can turn the pleasurable activity
of drinking

457
00:26:09,311 --> 00:26:10,520
into a repulsive one

458
00:26:11,104 --> 00:26:14,107
by pairing it with noxious smells
nausea-inducing medication

459
00:26:14,983 --> 00:26:16,526
low-grade electric shock.

460
00:26:17,069 --> 00:26:19,988
Of course, I record all my
sessions on a hard drive

461
00:26:20,113 --> 00:26:21,823
for insurance reasons, so...

462
00:26:24,076 --> 00:26:25,118
Uh... ah, here we go.

463
00:26:26,078 --> 00:26:27,662
"He's blowing .20."

464
00:26:28,163 --> 00:26:31,249
- "150 over 90. We should stop now."
- "He's okay."

465
00:26:31,458 --> 00:26:34,628
- Who is that nurse there?
- Uh, Lailah Bloom.

466
00:26:35,003 --> 00:26:37,172
Registered nurse. Ten years E.R.
experience behind her.

467
00:26:37,506 --> 00:26:39,382
She monitors my patients
every step of the way.

468
00:26:39,758 --> 00:26:42,010
We have very strict safety protocols.

469
00:26:42,135 --> 00:26:44,429
- "How you feeling, Benjamin?"
- "Beautiful."

470
00:26:45,555 --> 00:26:47,390
"Uh, sleepy."

471
00:26:48,558 --> 00:26:49,684
"I love this guy."

472
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,270
"All right, you can turn
the camera off now."

473
00:26:53,355 --> 00:26:54,439
"Let's get you home."

474
00:26:57,359 --> 00:26:58,985
As you can see, he was perfectly fine.

475
00:26:59,486 --> 00:27:02,072
After treatment, I drove Benjamin
back to his apartment.

476
00:27:02,364 --> 00:27:04,241
You were inside his home
the night he was killed.

477
00:27:04,574 --> 00:27:06,451
I make sure all my patients
get home safely.

478
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:13,667
What I offer here is a very personal,
hands-on therapy.

479
00:27:13,792 --> 00:27:15,836
It's the only way to make effective change
in people's lives.

480
00:27:15,961 --> 00:27:17,420
That and call girls.

481
00:27:17,546 --> 00:27:19,256
It's an interesting way
to drum up business.

482
00:27:19,422 --> 00:27:22,134
What you see as a call girl,
I see as a marketing expert

483
00:27:22,467 --> 00:27:25,345
with keen insights into the needs
and desires of my clientele.

484
00:27:26,888 --> 00:27:28,974
I focus on highly driven professionals.

485
00:27:33,979 --> 00:27:36,231
- Give us a few minutes?
- Sorry.

486
00:27:38,525 --> 00:27:41,236
Men like Benjamin have more to lose
if they can't control their urges.

487
00:27:41,778 --> 00:27:44,906
Before you trash my methods,
talk to my patients.

488
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:49,035
My success rate is higher than any
alcohol treatment center in the state.

489
00:27:49,911 --> 00:27:51,329
Excuse me. I need to make a call.

490
00:27:52,622 --> 00:27:54,332
And I'd like to see that entire video.

491
00:28:00,463 --> 00:28:03,049
Lailah, right? You okay?

492
00:28:03,425 --> 00:28:04,467
Fine.

493
00:28:06,845 --> 00:28:07,888
No, you're not.

494
00:28:09,306 --> 00:28:10,348
Talk to me.

495
00:28:13,393 --> 00:28:16,521
Did Mr. Wilder tell you what happened
after I turned off the camera?

496
00:28:19,900 --> 00:28:21,276
Benjamin passed out.

497
00:28:22,485 --> 00:28:25,238
His breathing was shallow,
his temperature was dropping.

498
00:28:25,363 --> 00:28:27,699
- Alcohol poisoning?
- Yes.

499
00:28:28,450 --> 00:28:31,036
I told Mr. Wilder we should get
Benjamin to a doctor...

500
00:28:31,411 --> 00:28:32,621
a medical doctor.

501
00:28:33,872 --> 00:28:37,292
But he said he had it under control
and they left.

502
00:28:37,417 --> 00:28:39,211
Has anything like that ever happened
here before?

503
00:28:41,963 --> 00:28:46,009
Look, I think Mr. Wilder
is a great man, okay?

504
00:28:46,176 --> 00:28:47,594
I grew up with alcoholic parents

505
00:28:47,719 --> 00:28:50,639
so I'm a big believer
in pushing limits to find a cure.

506
00:28:52,098 --> 00:28:53,141
But now...

507
00:28:54,559 --> 00:28:55,685
I don't know.

508
00:28:56,478 --> 00:28:57,562
Thanks for talking to me.

509
00:29:00,774 --> 00:29:03,610
Lailah said Ripple was showing
signs of alcohol poisoning.

510
00:29:03,860 --> 00:29:06,488
The coroner told me that's consistent
with what he found at autopsy.

511
00:29:06,655 --> 00:29:08,406
Okay, so Jack Wilder
drives Ripple home.

512
00:29:08,531 --> 00:29:11,159
Maybe Ripple passes out,
Wilder can't revive him

513
00:29:11,284 --> 00:29:14,246
so he stages a suicide
rather than risk losing it all.

514
00:29:14,663 --> 00:29:15,747
There's only one problem.

515
00:29:15,872 --> 00:29:17,791
- The evidence is circumstantial.
- All of it.

516
00:29:17,916 --> 00:29:19,542
I don't even think we have enough
for a search warrant.

517
00:29:20,168 --> 00:29:22,587
What kind of character witness
do you think Lailah would make in court?

518
00:29:23,088 --> 00:29:26,925
She does feel loyalty for Wilder.
I checked her employment history.

519
00:29:27,050 --> 00:29:29,928
She left a $70,000 job
at Sacramento General

520
00:29:30,053 --> 00:29:31,554
two months ago to work for him.

521
00:29:31,846 --> 00:29:34,307
On the other hand, both her parents
were alcoholic.

522
00:29:34,432 --> 00:29:36,851
I think that's where
her real sympathy lies.

523
00:29:36,977 --> 00:29:38,645
Parents were alcoholic?

524
00:29:40,814 --> 00:29:43,316
Her mom died in a car crash.

525
00:29:43,441 --> 00:29:44,484
She was drunk.

526
00:29:44,609 --> 00:29:48,071
Cirrhosis of the liver took her dad.
Also alcohol-related.

527
00:29:48,405 --> 00:29:52,200
Chance has thrust our way
a very sordid and vexing problem.

528
00:29:54,202 --> 00:29:55,370
But have no fear.

529
00:29:56,830 --> 00:29:58,748
- We don't.
- I do.

530
00:29:59,332 --> 00:30:00,375
What's your plan?

531
00:30:09,107 --> 00:30:11,109
Thank you for, uh, fitting me in.

532
00:30:11,734 --> 00:30:13,403
Our corporate retreat is in two days.

533
00:30:13,861 --> 00:30:15,571
That's why it's crucial to get started now.

534
00:30:16,781 --> 00:30:18,116
You're sure you've had
nothing to eat today?

535
00:30:18,241 --> 00:30:20,493
No, no, no.
To stressed to eat.

536
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,788
They say it's a rafting trip.
It's really just an excuse

537
00:30:23,913 --> 00:30:26,416
to drink like Germans for a weekend.

538
00:30:28,418 --> 00:30:30,670
I can't afford to slip. I'm up for C.E.O.

539
00:30:31,087 --> 00:30:33,548
Don't worry, Patrick.
All behavior is learned.

540
00:30:33,881 --> 00:30:35,466
And with my help, soon

541
00:30:35,716 --> 00:30:37,927
your unwanted behavior
will be unlearned.

542
00:30:38,511 --> 00:30:39,887
Now I want you to take this dial.

543
00:30:40,847 --> 00:30:44,350
And select a level of current
that's uncomfortable but not painful.

544
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:51,482
Tickles.

545
00:30:51,941 --> 00:30:53,568
Oh. Okay.
Touchy.

546
00:30:54,318 --> 00:30:57,196
Tonight, we are gonna take the fun
out of drinking for you.

547
00:31:00,616 --> 00:31:02,702
Lailah, pour the man some whiskey.

548
00:31:07,248 --> 00:31:08,291
Bottoms up.

549
00:31:18,009 --> 00:31:19,385
Oh. I felt that.

550
00:31:21,304 --> 00:31:22,388
I did feel that.

551
00:31:22,763 --> 00:31:25,975
Our goal is to associate alcohol
and all of its social rituals

552
00:31:26,267 --> 00:31:29,729
with the unpleasant sensation of electricity
running through your body.

553
00:31:30,980 --> 00:31:32,023
Okay.

554
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:51,375
Good, good.

555
00:31:51,501 --> 00:31:52,543
Taxi.

556
00:31:52,919 --> 00:31:54,128
How you feeling, Patrick?

557
00:31:54,462 --> 00:31:56,839
Well, Lailah, I'm probably
not going to remember much

558
00:31:56,964 --> 00:31:58,758
about tonight, so let's just
take a moment

559
00:31:58,883 --> 00:32:01,052
to remember this moment
forever together.

560
00:32:03,179 --> 00:32:05,306
You have brown eyes
and you're wearing earrings.

561
00:32:06,182 --> 00:32:07,433
I'll never forget that.

562
00:32:08,100 --> 00:32:10,311
- Time to raise the current.
- Really?

563
00:32:11,729 --> 00:32:13,773
These restraints will make sure
you don't accidentally

564
00:32:13,898 --> 00:32:15,274
dislodge your electrodes.

565
00:32:15,942 --> 00:32:18,736
We don't wanna dislodge any
electrodes, do we, doc?

566
00:32:19,779 --> 00:32:20,947
Ready for the next one?

567
00:32:21,072 --> 00:32:23,282
Uh... here's to sobriety.

568
00:32:38,130 --> 00:32:39,590
This is the last one.

569
00:32:41,092 --> 00:32:42,134
Are you okay?

570
00:32:42,885 --> 00:32:46,013
He's fine, Lailah.
He's just a little tipsy.

571
00:32:46,806 --> 00:32:48,474
This is the most important one.

572
00:32:48,933 --> 00:32:50,059
Please continue.

573
00:33:02,697 --> 00:33:07,368
Oh. Okay.

574
00:33:08,578 --> 00:33:10,830
I feel like... I can move.

575
00:33:12,081 --> 00:33:13,416
The air doesn't stop me.

576
00:33:17,336 --> 00:33:19,630
- His eyes are pretty red.
- Yours are glazed.

577
00:33:19,755 --> 00:33:20,965
You been eating doughnuts?

578
00:33:21,841 --> 00:33:24,468
The patient's blood pressure is too low.
Something's wrong.

579
00:33:24,719 --> 00:33:28,431
No, it's okay. You set me free
of all my pain.

580
00:33:28,723 --> 00:33:31,267
- Irregular heartbeat. Skin's ice.
- No, no, no. It's impossible.

581
00:33:31,392 --> 00:33:32,476
I calculated his body weight.

582
00:33:32,602 --> 00:33:35,313
This man will go into cardiac arrest
without emergency medical care.

583
00:33:35,563 --> 00:33:37,690
Go call 9-1-1. Go!

584
00:33:44,947 --> 00:33:46,240
I'll set you free.

585
00:33:47,033 --> 00:33:48,075
Forever.

586
00:33:59,587 --> 00:34:00,630
Gotcha.

587
00:34:01,172 --> 00:34:02,423
Whoa, little head spin there.

588
00:34:03,424 --> 00:34:05,885
You can't be conscious. Your vitals...

589
00:34:06,344 --> 00:34:08,095
Little biofeedback trick.

590
00:34:08,346 --> 00:34:09,972
Well, not so little when you're drunk.

591
00:34:12,016 --> 00:34:15,895
- Cat's in the bag. Come on in.
- What are you talking about?

592
00:34:16,187 --> 00:34:17,313
I'm a cop.

593
00:34:17,730 --> 00:34:21,525
Well, cop-adjacent.
This place is surrounded.

594
00:34:26,322 --> 00:34:28,783
It's a complex little transmitter.

595
00:34:28,908 --> 00:34:32,203
Surveillance van out the front
full of people with large guns.

596
00:34:32,745 --> 00:34:34,080
You are in trouble.

597
00:34:38,542 --> 00:34:39,669
You're lying.

598
00:34:40,961 --> 00:34:45,925
Let me guess. 190-proof alcohol.
Same gut-rot you shot into Ripple.

599
00:34:46,550 --> 00:34:48,552
The good doctor here thinks
you're an angel.

600
00:34:49,053 --> 00:34:50,137
I am an angel.

601
00:34:50,888 --> 00:34:52,682
Yeah. An angel of death.

602
00:34:54,767 --> 00:34:58,521
You know, I had a hunch
soon as I found out about your pants.

603
00:35:00,231 --> 00:35:01,982
Pardon me. Your parents.

604
00:35:03,651 --> 00:35:05,111
You've experienced a lot of pain.

605
00:35:05,403 --> 00:35:08,572
Alcohol causes pain. Loneliness.

606
00:35:08,698 --> 00:35:11,701
So it was you that overdosed Ripple.
It wasn't Wilder.

607
00:35:12,743 --> 00:35:13,911
He left and you went in.

608
00:35:14,036 --> 00:35:15,871
How did you get into
Benjamin's apartment?

609
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,123
When Benjamin was drunk

610
00:35:17,248 --> 00:35:18,916
he mentioned where
he kept his spare key.

611
00:35:21,043 --> 00:35:23,295
"Poor thing was hurting
so badly inside."

612
00:35:26,132 --> 00:35:28,342
Benjamin, wake up. It's important.

613
00:35:28,467 --> 00:35:30,636
- Uh...
- there are children outside.

614
00:35:30,845 --> 00:35:32,304
- Oh...
- they wanna see Santa.

615
00:35:32,430 --> 00:35:34,473
Oh, can't let the children down.

616
00:35:42,148 --> 00:35:43,441
I'm not feeling so good.

617
00:35:43,649 --> 00:35:46,527
- All you gotta do is wave at them.
- Okay.

618
00:35:46,652 --> 00:35:49,321
You see 'em down there?
Maybe if you Lean a little further.

619
00:35:50,406 --> 00:35:52,199
- Oh
- You see 'em?

620
00:36:00,708 --> 00:36:02,293
Do you know the one part of the body

621
00:36:02,418 --> 00:36:05,504
that coroners rarely inspect
for needle marks?

622
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:10,801
Inside the navel.

623
00:36:11,677 --> 00:36:17,016
Uh, cat's in the bag,
and the bag's almost in the river!

624
00:36:17,141 --> 00:36:21,687
If I end your suffering now
Jack will be blamed for both deaths.

625
00:36:22,563 --> 00:36:24,774
And let's face it,
Jack needs to be stopped.

626
00:36:25,357 --> 00:36:26,859
He's a little crazy.

627
00:36:29,904 --> 00:36:31,030
Drop the needle!

628
00:36:31,405 --> 00:36:32,782
Put it down! Now!

629
00:36:35,034 --> 00:36:36,744
I'm sorry. We didn't mean
to cut it this close.

630
00:36:36,869 --> 00:36:38,954
- This place is a maze.
- Turn around.

631
00:36:41,207 --> 00:36:44,126
- Are you all right?
- Oh, yeah. I'm fine. I'm still home.

632
00:36:45,377 --> 00:36:46,587
Would you take me drunk?

633
00:36:50,007 --> 00:36:52,301
- Mr. LaRoche?
- What's going on in here?

634
00:36:52,593 --> 00:36:55,638
I've come to question Jane
about the murder of Todd Johnson.

635
00:36:55,805 --> 00:36:59,934
Unless he answers my questions,
his status as a CBI consultant

636
00:37:00,059 --> 00:37:01,811
will fall under immediate review.

637
00:37:01,977 --> 00:37:03,813
No more waiting, no more ducking.

638
00:37:03,979 --> 00:37:05,564
No, you don't. Not now. No.

639
00:37:05,981 --> 00:37:08,692
No, it's all right, Lisbon.
I got this one. I got him.

640
00:37:09,151 --> 00:37:10,861
Come on. Fire away.

641
00:37:13,739 --> 00:37:14,824
- I got it.
- Okay.

642
00:37:29,713 --> 00:37:33,300
Agent Lisbon states that before
Todd Johnson was set on fire

643
00:37:33,425 --> 00:37:37,388
he indicated to her that he had
a secret he wanted to tell you

644
00:37:37,805 --> 00:37:41,141
- and you alone.
- We all have secrets.

645
00:37:42,476 --> 00:37:45,396
Most of them are quite unremarkable
once revealed.

646
00:37:48,566 --> 00:37:50,609
What's your secret, Mr. Laroosh?

647
00:37:51,735 --> 00:37:52,778
LaRoche.

648
00:37:53,529 --> 00:37:54,572
Pardon me.

649
00:37:55,489 --> 00:37:56,824
I have no secrets.

650
00:37:57,575 --> 00:37:58,617
None?

651
00:38:02,621 --> 00:38:09,420
- You have a very keen, speculative mind.
- You flatter me.

652
00:38:12,506 --> 00:38:15,301
What do you think Johnson
wanted to tell you?

653
00:38:15,509 --> 00:38:18,554
What was his secret?
Your best guess.

654
00:38:18,762 --> 00:38:19,805
Best guess.

655
00:38:20,097 --> 00:38:21,640
Uh, same sad old story.

656
00:38:23,517 --> 00:38:25,311
Just wanted to explain himself.

657
00:38:27,062 --> 00:38:30,065
Wanted to show someone
that he was human.

658
00:38:31,525 --> 00:38:36,196
He's just a lonely soul trying to get by
like you or me.

659
00:38:37,364 --> 00:38:40,910
- Why did he have to tell you this?
- Because he's a cop killer...

660
00:38:41,327 --> 00:38:47,249
In a cop house, full of cop hens
and cop chickens.

661
00:38:47,833 --> 00:38:48,959
That's very amusing.

662
00:38:49,460 --> 00:38:50,586
And I'm not a cop.

663
00:38:51,712 --> 00:38:54,006
But you would be very surprised

664
00:38:54,131 --> 00:38:57,426
how unsympathetic policemen
can be... and women.

665
00:39:03,724 --> 00:39:04,767
Thank you.

666
00:39:04,892 --> 00:39:05,935
Oh, no. Thank you.

667
00:39:06,685 --> 00:39:07,728
It was fun.

668
00:39:08,479 --> 00:39:09,521
We'll be in touch.

669
00:39:12,232 --> 00:39:14,985
Oh, if you, uh... care to share

670
00:39:15,110 --> 00:39:16,904
any of the developments
on the case with me

671
00:39:17,029 --> 00:39:18,948
then I won't tell anyone.

672
00:39:19,698 --> 00:39:22,284
- Why would you wanna know?
- I love a mystery.

673
00:39:24,870 --> 00:39:26,121
It's one of my failings.

674
00:39:39,969 --> 00:39:42,554
- Ah. Patrick?
- Ah, Virgil.

675
00:39:43,597 --> 00:39:45,641
Meet May. May, this is Virgil.

676
00:39:47,518 --> 00:39:48,978
- Hello, May.
- Hi.

677
00:39:51,981 --> 00:39:55,359
Uh... oh, uh, um, a moment alone,
please, Jane?

678
00:39:55,859 --> 00:39:57,361
- Will you excuse us?
- Sure.

679
00:40:00,114 --> 00:40:01,615
Excuse me. A little parched.

680
00:40:03,826 --> 00:40:04,952
Thank you for meeting me here.

681
00:40:05,828 --> 00:40:08,831
You look terrible.
What did you do last night?

682
00:40:08,956 --> 00:40:10,416
Ah, it's all a little gauzy.

683
00:40:10,541 --> 00:40:13,419
I hope you don't mind
I brought May along.

684
00:40:13,836 --> 00:40:15,337
Uh, you know, what's her story?

685
00:40:15,462 --> 00:40:17,131
Oh, come on. Ask her yourself.

686
00:40:19,591 --> 00:40:22,678
Listen, I'd, uh...
I'd like to convey my gratitude.

687
00:40:22,803 --> 00:40:26,348
- Easy, cowboy. You just met her.
- I'm not talking about that.

688
00:40:27,016 --> 00:40:29,101
What you said about that fish.

689
00:40:29,893 --> 00:40:33,063
You opened my eyes to some ugly
truths that I've been avoiding.

690
00:40:37,818 --> 00:40:40,904
LaRoche's suspect list, secured
through back channels

691
00:40:41,030 --> 00:40:42,364
and personal favors.

692
00:40:43,449 --> 00:40:45,534
LaRoche has no idea I have it...

693
00:40:49,621 --> 00:40:50,664
Thank you.

694
00:40:54,793 --> 00:40:56,503
- You need anything else, let me know.
- I will.

695
00:40:56,712 --> 00:40:58,881
I have to go.
Uh, could you do me a favor?

696
00:40:59,089 --> 00:41:01,133
Could you extend my apologies to May?

697
00:41:01,258 --> 00:41:02,885
Perhaps you'll sit with her
and have some lunch?

698
00:41:03,093 --> 00:41:05,596
I can do that, I think.

699
00:41:08,599 --> 00:41:09,641
Any tips?

700
00:41:10,017 --> 00:41:13,062
Uh, yes. You might wanna
consider growing a beard.

701
00:41:19,026 --> 00:41:26,533
"May your days be merry and bright"

702
00:41:30,162 --> 00:41:38,253
"And may all your Christmases be wild"

